WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Tesla's Robotaxi fleet reached 1 million unsupervised miles, giving regulators a concrete data set to evaluate the system. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 594. Tesla plans to turn on continuous Robotaxi operation within roughly 30 days. The move follows recent unsupervised driving tests on public roads. Regulators will now see round the clock fleet data instead of limited windows. Production and supervision metrics are expected to improve

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:51.720
under the new schedule. The change removes time-of-day restrictions that have limited data collection so far. Continuous operation will also let Tesla measure how the fleet handles overnight demand patterns in Austin. A steering wheel-free vehicle carried passengers through Austin streets with no visible driver input. The test used the production cybercab configuration.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:01:17.080
Observers noted the absence of pedals and traditional controls. This marks the first public demonstration of the wheel-free model in city traffic. The ride occurred on regular urban routes rather than closed courses. Passengers experienced the full sequence from pickup to drop off without any manual intervention. The doors continue sensing objects after the closed cycle begins and can reverse instantly if blocked.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:37.440
The same logic applies to the opening sequence, switching to a manual hold command when needed. No driver is present to intervene so the vehicle must handle all edge cases. Emergency mechanical release remains available if power is lost. The system checks the path before any movement starts and keeps monitoring throughout the motion.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:02:03.200
This layered approach replaces the visual oversight a human driver would normally provide. Federal regulators open to review hours after the Austin debut over FMVSS certification questions. The probe focuses on whether the wheel-free design meets existing standards. Tesla must now supply documentation on safety systems that replace traditional controls. Outcomes could affect the timeline for wider deployment.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:15.900
The investigation examines how the vehicle satisfies requirements originally written for cars with steering wheels and pedals. Tesla is expected to submit detailed engineering data on the new sensor and actuator suite.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:36.920
Windrose, an electric truck maker positioned against Tesla semi, has seen most of its China team depart. The departures follow a period of rapid hiring aimed at scaling production. Remaining staff must now manage both development and supplier relationships. The loss could slow the company's effort to enter the North American market.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:03:03.540
Key engineering and procurement roles are among those vacated. The reduced head count directly impacts the pace of prototype validation and component sourcing. The three row model YL received EPA range figures up to seven miles above Tesla's original estimates. The larger heavier vehicle now exceeds the standard model Y in tested range. Buyers gain a clearer picture of real world capability for family use.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:26.720
Tesla has not yet adjusted pricing or production targets based on the new numbers. The improved ratings reflect efficiency gains from updated power train calibration and aerodynamic tweaks. Fleet operators considering the model now have firmer data for root planning. The partnership recovers minerals through hydro metallurgical processing and feeds them back into new cell production.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:38.200
Closed loop recovery reduces reliance on virgin materials for both vehicle and energy storage batteries. Tesla supplies end-of-life packs while redwood handles refining at scale.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:48.660
Yield improvements directly affect long-term material cost curves. The process targets lithium, nickel and cobalt recovery rates that support future production growth.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:04:07.900
Material return to the supply chain lowers exposure to commodity price swings. Battery electric vehicles outsold pure petrol cars in Australia for the first time last month. The model Y led all models in registrations. The result reflects stronger supply of right hand drive units and continued price positioning.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:18.040
Petrol hybrid sales remained strong but did not offset the electric shift. The crossover body style continues to dominate buyer preferences across major cities.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:28.540
Tesla's local inventory levels supported immediate delivery for many customers. Production of the third generation mega pack started at the Texas energy factory this week.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:38.980
The updated unit incorporates higher density cells and revised thermal management. Utility customers gain additional capacity per footprint compared with prior versions.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:50.000
Output will feed both domestic projects and export orders already in backlog. The new thermal architecture supports faster charge and discharge cycles during peak grid events.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:00.380
Early units are undergoing final validation before shipment to initial utility partners. The company has targeted an unsupervised FSD release for the current quarter.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:11.980
Regulators in multiple markets have not yet granted the required approvals. Software versions continue to advance in supervised mode but the gap between testing and commercial deployment remains.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:23.220
Any extension would push revenue recognition for the feature into 2027. The timeline depends on completing safety validation reports required by state and federal agencies.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:34.540
Internal milestones for miles per intervention continue to improve in supervised fleets. A court rejected Tesla's motion to end a lawsuit tied to a reposted image on the platform.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:45.420
The claim centers on unauthorized use of protected material in a corporate social post. Tesla argued fair use and platform immunity but the judge allowed the case to proceed.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:55.280
The ruling sets a precedent for how companies handle third party content on their own channels. Legal teams must now prepare discovery and potential settlement discussions.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:06.260
The matter adds administrative overhead during a period of intense product and regulatory activity. The fleet accumulated the mileage entirely without human supervision during testing.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:16.600
The figure provides regulators with a larger statistical base than previous disclosures. Tesla highlighted the data as evidence of system maturity ahead of broader rollout.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:27.340
Future updates will track whether the rate of unsupervised miles continues to accelerate. The milestone covers varied urban and highway conditions in the Austin operating area.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:39.480
Analysts expect the data set to feature in upcoming safety submissions to NHTSA. The butterfly doors incorporate layered sensors and control logic refined across several vehicle programs.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:46.560
Engineers iterated on both mechanical geometry and software response curves before reaching the current implementation.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:58.940
The design now handles edge cases that earlier prototypes could not manage reliably. Multiple hardware revisions were required to achieve consistent performance across temperature extremes and passenger loads.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:06.100
The final version integrates with the vehicle's central compute for coordinated responses during pickup and drop off sequences.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.820
A 22-inch touchscreen supports theater, music, and gaming applications during rides.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:23.240
V5 Starlink hardware will be added to maintain connectivity in areas without strong cellular coverage. The interior is positioned as a flexible space rather than a simple transit pod.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:35.720
Passengers can switch between productivity tools and entertainment without leaving the vehicle. The connectivity upgrade targets consistent streaming performance on longer suburban routes where ground networks can drop.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:47.400
French authorities are conducting supervised tests of the system on public roads. The trials evaluate camera-based perception in mixed traffic and varied weather conditions typical of European routes.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:53.380
Results will feed into ongoing discussions about harmonized autonomous vehicle rules across the EU.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:08:03.300
Tesla is one of several manufacturers participating in the program. Data collected will help shape future type approval processes for vehicles without traditional controls.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:13.020
There is a challenge worth discussing on the legal side. A court allowed the lawsuit to continue after rejecting Tesla's fair use and platform immunity arguments.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:28.080
The case centers on a single reposted image rather than a broad policy issue. Tesla must now prepare a full defense or negotiate a settlement, adding legal cost at a time when regulatory scrutiny on autonomous vehicles is already high.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:34.420
The ruling could influence how the company manages third-party content across its corporate channels going forward.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:45.360
External counsel will review similar posts to reduce future exposure. Autonomous vehicles shift the safety burden from driver reaction time to sensor and software latency.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:55.280
Traditional cars rely on a human to notice an open door or a passenger still boarding, but a robot taxi must detect those conditions without any onboard observer.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:09:01.480
This forces every subsystem, including doors, to carry its own real-time verification layer.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:10.700
The requirement applies equally to opening and closing sequences, creating a continuous monitoring obligation that did not exist in driver-controlled vehicles.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:20.400
The cybercab door system illustrates the point. It keeps monitoring during the entire closed cycle and can reverse motion within milliseconds if an obstruction appears.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:29.380
The same logic governs opening, disabling automatic movement when the path is blocked, and requiring a deliberate hold to open command instead.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:34.540
These features add hardware and software complexity that conventional vehicles never needed.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:46.800
Validation now includes thousands of edge-case scenarios that previously fell to the driver. The added intelligence raises unit cost and validation effort, yet it is non-negotiable once the driver is removed.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:54.640
Before we go, the next round of unsupervised testing data should show whether overnight operation changes intervention rates in Austin.

